# {{ project_name }} on Google Cloud Functions

The generated directory contains the complete function source: `main.py`,
`_routes.py`, `_pywire_build/`, and `requirements.txt`. Deploy from the project
root, changing only the GCP project, region, and runtime if needed:

```sh
gcloud functions deploy {{ project_name }} \
  --gen2 \
  --runtime=python312 \
  --region=us-central1 \
  --source=.pywire/deploy/gcp_functions \
  --entry-point=pywire \
  --trigger-http \
  --set-env-vars=PYWIRE_SECRET_KEY="$(python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))')" \
  --allow-unauthenticated
```
